@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Google sign-in / explicit linking: authorization-code flow with PKCE
hide footbox
autonumber
actor User
participant Browser
participant "auth.py\n<<route functions>>" as Auth
participant "AuthStore / identity SQLite" as Store
participant "Google OAuth / JWKS" as Google

activate User
User -> Browser : Continue with Google / Link Google
activate Browser
Browser -> Auth : GET /auth/google/start [link=true]
activate Auth
Auth -> Store : store expiring state, browser digest, verifier and nonce
activate Store
Store --> Auth : stored; signed-in owner if explicit linking
deactivate Store
Auth --> Browser : 302 authorization URL + HttpOnly state cookie
deactivate Auth
Browser -> Google : authorize with code challenge, state and nonce
activate Google
note over Google : Human account selection and consent are outside automated mock acceptance.
Google --> Browser : redirect with authorization code and state, or denial
deactivate Google
Browser -> Auth : GET /auth/google/callback
activate Auth
Auth -> Store : consume matching state and browser binding
activate Store
Store --> Auth : one-time verifier + nonce + optional linking owner
deactivate Store
alt valid callback state
  Auth -> Google : exchange code + PKCE verifier + configured client
  activate Google
  Google --> Auth : ID token or provider error
  deactivate Google
  Auth -> Google : obtain signing keys
  activate Google
  Google --> Auth : JWKS or provider error
  deactivate Google
  Auth -> Auth : verify signature, issuer, audience, expiry,\nnonce and verified email
  activate Auth
  Auth --> Auth : validated claims or rejection
  deactivate Auth
  alt verified claims
    Auth -> Store : resolve subject / create account / explicitly link
    activate Store
    note over Store : Equal email alone never links a password account.\nExplicit linking must match the authenticated owner.
    Store --> Auth : account or link-required conflict
    deactivate Store
    opt account accepted
      Auth -> Store : create session
      activate Store
      Store --> Auth : new random session
      deactivate Store
    end
  else invalid identity token
    note over Auth : No identity or session is created.
  end
else missing, expired or replayed state
  note over Auth : No provider exchange is authorized.
end
Auth --> Browser : redirect + session cookie, or safe account error
deactivate Auth
Browser --> User : signed-in workspace / actionable sign-in outcome
deactivate Browser
deactivate User
legend bottom
  Redirects are HTTP replies; following them begins a new request.
  Code, verifier, nonce and credentials are not written to browser storage.
  Query values are redacted from application access logs.
endlegend
@enduml
